From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:28:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 473/488] [DS4.1] Verification: the insertion caps counts at
 the dead-row cut; chunk offsets without a launch

The rejection sampler capped each request's count at its dead-row cut plus one
with two torch launches (dead_row_cut + 1, torch.minimum) after verification.
The resampled-token insertion, which stores every count, now stores the capped
one in the same store (insert_kernel's limited variant, declared beside the
uncapped one when the step can have dead rows); the token still goes where the
uncapped count puts it.

The first verification chunk takes the batch's offsets as a view instead of
subtracting 0 from them; a later chunk (never adaptive) uploads its offsets
from the host. A single chunk's sink alternates are returned as they are, not
concatenated.

benchmark_resampled_token.py --dead-rows times the capped insertion against
the uncapped one plus torch's cap.
